+# Aegis — Apple Core ML, SDK & Federated Patch
+
+This unified patch adds a compact, operator-oriented scaffold to support:
+- Core ML conversion CI & tools (convert_to_coreml.py, CI workflow)
+- MLflow logging of Core ML artifacts & pseudo energy metrics
+- Server-side signing via Vault Transit (receipt_signer_vault)
+- On-device SDK skeleton (Swift): ConsentManager, RetrievalGuardClient, Prefilled A2A UI, SecureEnclave signer, Device attestation helpers, Federated client stub
+- Federated orchestrator (Flask) with simple secure aggregation + DP noise
+- Observability hooks: Grafana dashboard JSON and Prometheus ServiceMonitors (if using Prometheus Operator)
+- App Store/enterprise takedown adapter that records takedown tasks and posts to MCP
+
+Operator notes:
+- CI conversion should run on macOS runners if you need true Core ML runtime validation. The conversion script uses coremltools and can run on Linux for ONNX->CoreML conversions but latency/energy tests should be done on macOS machines with Core ML runtime.
+- Configure Vault (VAULT_ADDR, TRANSIT_KEY_NAME) and Rekor (REKOR_URL) before enabling receipt_signer_vault.
+- Deploy the federated orchestrator behind ingress, configure TLS and authentication for clients, and adjust DP parameters (epsilon) for your privacy budget.
+- The iOS SDK files are skeletons; incorporate them into an Xcode Swift Package and wire to your app's UI flows. The Secure Enclave signer should be used with care and tested across device models.
+- The takedown adapter creates operator tasks in /data/takedown_tasks for manual App Store / enterprise actions — integrate with your internal ticketing or App Store Connect APIs as needed.
+
+Security / Privacy reminders:
+- Keep VAULT_TOKEN out of repos; prefer Kubernetes auth or Vault Agent.
+- Device attestation flows require server coordination and verification — implement server-side verification of DeviceCheck / AppAttest tokens per Apple docs.
+- Federated client updates should be authenticated and rate-limited; do not accept arbitrary payloads in production.
+
